-- title:
--   Transitivity above varpi and reducedness for the blow-up chart
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, a natural number $M'\neq 0$ with $q\nmid M'$ (`hqM'`), and a prime $\ell$ with $\ell\equiv 11\pmod{12}$ (`hℓ12`) and $\ell\mid M'$ (`hℓM'`). Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero and $\zeta\in L$ a primitive $q$-th root of unity (`hζ`) admitting a ring homomorphism $\iota\colon L\to\mathbb C$ with $\iota\zeta=e^{2\pi i/q}$ (`hι`). Let $H_1\le(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^{\times}$ be, by `hH₁`, the intersection of [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH q M'`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelJacobian.html#L22) — the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^{\times}\to(\mathbb Z/q)^{\times}$, i.e. the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$ — with the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^{\times}\to(\mathbb Z/\ell)^{\times}$. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L\subseteq L((t))$ which, by `hK`, is [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.xHFunctionField (q ^ 2 * M') H₁)`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103): the $L$-subfield of $L((t))$ generated by the image, under the coefficientwise map [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81), of the $q$-expansion function field over $\mathbb Q$ attached to [`CohCarrier.GammaH (q ^ 2 * M') H₁`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L133).
--
--   Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$, henselian local with algebraically closed residue field, carrying an $A$-algebra structure on $K$ compatible with $L$, with $q\in\mathfrak m_A$ (`hAq`) and $\zeta$ in the image of $A$ (`hζA`). Let $j\in K$, $j\neq 0$, whose Laurent expansion is the image of the $q$-expansion [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) of the modular $j$-function (`hj`). Let $\varpi$ generate $\mathfrak m_A$ (`hϖ`) and let $\varpi_t\in A$ satisfy $\varpi_t^{q^2-1}=qu$ for some unit $u$ (`hϖt`). Throughout, `chartAlgFin A K j` is the $A$-subalgebra of elements of $K$ integral over $A[j]$, and [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236) is the pushout of the two chart spectra along the middle chart, with structure morphism `toBase` to $\mathrm{Spec}\,A$.
--
--   Data on the chart: a maximal ideal $y$ of `chartAlgFin A K j` (`hy`) containing the image of $\varpi$ (`hϖy`), supersingular at $y$ in the sense of `hss`: for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from the chart algebra with kernel $y$, the value $\varphi(j)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), the set of elements $j_0$ such that every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\Omega$ with $j$-invariant $j_0$ has no nonzero $q$-torsion point.
--
--   Data on the model: a point $z$ of the two-chart model, the germ $\varpi_z$ at $z$ of the pullback of $\varpi$ along `toBase` (`hϖz`), assumed to lie in the maximal ideal of the stalk at $z$ (`hz`); a point $y'$ of `XFin = Spec (chartAlgFin A K j)` with `ιFin`-image $z$ (`hy'`), satisfying the same supersingularity condition at `y'.asIdeal` (`hss'`), and with `y'.asIdeal = y` (`hy'y`).
--
--   Data on the local model: a complete discrete valuation domain $W_1$, a ring homomorphism $\sigma_1\colon A\to W_1$ with $\mathfrak m_{W_1}=(\sigma_1\varpi)$ (`hσ₁`), power series $f_1,u_1,v_1\in W_1[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $u_1,v_1$ units (`hu₁`, `hv₁`) and $f_1\equiv X_0X_1^{q}-X_0^{q}X_1$ modulo $(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$ (`hf₁`, the Drinfeld form [`DrinfeldCurve.LocalChart.drinfeldForm q W₁`](def/DrinfeldCurve_LocalChart.html#L18)), and a ring isomorphism $e_1$ from the adic completion of the stalk at $z$ onto
--   $$S:=W_1[[X_0,X_1]]\big/\big(C(\sigma_1(\varpi_t^{q+1}))\,v_1-f_1u_1\big).$$
--   Write `toC` for the completion map from the stalk, `mkS` for the quotient map onto $S$, and `germY` for the ring homomorphism from `chartAlgFin A K j` to the stalk at $z$ obtained from the germ at $z$ on the `ιFin`-image of the chart.
--
--   The hypothesis `hW₁` is a conjunction of seven clauses: (i) $e_1\circ{}$`toC` carries the germ of the pullback of $a\in A$ to `mkS (C (σ₁ a))`; (ii) for every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ and every $\tau\in\mathrm{Aut}_L(K)$ with `IsLevelAutAt L q ζ q (q^2*M') H₁ γ⁻¹ K τ`, the automorphism $\tau$ maps `chartAlgFin A K j` into itself; (iii) if moreover $\gamma_{11}\equiv 1\pmod\ell$, then the restriction of $\tau$ to the chart algebra is congruent to the identity modulo `y'.asIdeal`; (iv) for every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ and every such $\tau$ preserving the chart algebra and congruent to the identity modulo `y'.asIdeal`, there exist a ring automorphism $\theta$ of $S$, an element $c\in W_1$ and a matrix $M\in M_2(W_1)$ such that $\theta$ intertwines, through $e_1\circ{}$`toC`$\circ{}$`germY`, the identity with the restriction of $\tau$; $\theta$ fixes every constant `mkS (C w)`; $\theta(\mathrm{mk}_S X_{j})\equiv\sum_i \mathrm{mk}_S(C(M_{ij})X_i)$ modulo the square of the ideal generated by $\mathrm{mk}_S X_0,\mathrm{mk}_S X_1$; $c^{q+1}\equiv 1$ and $M_{ij}\equiv c\,\gamma_{ij}$ modulo $\mathfrak m_{W_1}$ for all $i,j$; $c\equiv 1$ modulo $\mathfrak m_{W_1}$ whenever $\gamma_{11}\equiv 1\pmod \ell$; and $c\not\equiv 1$ modulo $\mathfrak m_{W_1}$ whenever $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)$ and $\tau$ is not the identity on $K$; (v) a separation clause: for integers $a_1,b_1,a_2,b_2$ and prime ideals $P_1,P_2$ of $S$, each omitting at least one of $\mathrm{mk}_S X_0,\mathrm{mk}_S X_1$, each containing $\mathrm{mk}_S(C(\sigma_1\varpi))$, and each containing an element $a_iX_0+b_iX_1+h$ with $h\in(X_0,X_1)^2$, if $q\nmid a_1b_2-a_2b_1$ then the contractions of $P_1$ and $P_2$ along $e_1\circ{}$`toC` to the stalk are distinct; (vi) for a prime $P$ of $S$ omitting at least one of $\mathrm{mk}_S X_0,\mathrm{mk}_S X_1$, containing $\mathrm{mk}_S(C(\sigma_1\varpi))$ and containing $1\cdot X_0+0\cdot X_1+h$ for some $h\in(X_0,X_1)^2$, an element $a$ of the chart algebra satisfies `toC (germY a)` $\in$ `Ideal.comap e₁ P` if and only if every Laurent coefficient of $a$ lies in the image of $\mathfrak m_A$ in $L$; (vii) an existence clause: the $q$-expansion [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L q`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18) lies in $K$ and in the chart algebra, and there are $a_0\in A$ with the corresponding difference in `y'.asIdeal`, an integer $e_0\ge 1$ and $h\in(X_0,X_1)^{e_0}$ such that for all $a,b\in W_1$ with at least one of $a,b$ a unit and $a^qb-ab^q\in\mathfrak m_{W_1}$ the sum $\sum_{i=0}^{e_0}\mathrm{coeff}_{(i,e_0-i)}(h)\,a^ib^{e_0-i}$ is a unit, and $e_1($`toC (germY (`$j_{q}$-element$-a_0))$ $=$ `mkS h`.
--
--   Finally, let $J$ be the ideal of `chartAlgFin A K j` which, by `hJ`, is the infimum of the ideals obtained as follows: for $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ and $\tau$ a level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$ preserving the chart algebra, pull back along the restriction of $\tau$ the contraction along $e_1\circ{}$`toC`$\circ{}$`germY` of the ideal of $S$ generated by $\mathrm{mk}_S(C(\sigma_1\varpi_t))$, $\mathrm{mk}_S X_0$, $\mathrm{mk}_S X_1$. Let $B$ be the $A$-subalgebra of $K$ which, by `hB`, is generated over `chartAlgFin A K j` by the set of $x\in K$ with $x\varpi_t\in J$, and let $W$ be a valuation subring of $K$ containing $B$ (`hBW`). The further hypotheses are: `hR1`, that `chartAlgFin A K j` $\le B$ and every element of $K$ is a quotient of two elements of $B$ with nonzero denominator; `hR2`, that $A\to B$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation and $B/(\varpi)$ has Krull dimension at most $1$; `hR3` (five clauses), that an element of $L$ lies in $W$ exactly when it comes from $A$, that $\mathfrak m_W$ is generated by the image of $\varpi$, that $W$ is a discrete valuation ring, that an element of the chart algebra lies in $y$ exactly when it lies in $\mathfrak m_W$, and that $W$ consists of the quotients $g/h$ with $g,h\in B$ and $h\notin\mathfrak m_W$; `hJstab` and `hBstab`, that for every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ and every level automorphism $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$ membership in $J$ is preserved by $\tau$ and $\tau(B)\subseteq B$; `hPid`, that an element of $B$ lies in $\mathfrak m_W$ exactly when it lies in the ideal of $B$ generated by the image of $y$; and `hJy`, `hϖtJ`, that $J\le y$ and the image of $\varpi_t$ lies in $J$. Here `IsLevelAutAt L q ζ q (q^2*M') H₁ γ⁻¹ K τ` means that for every weight $k$, every pair $f,g$ of modular forms of weight $k$ for the group attached to [`CohCarrier.GammaH (q^2*M') H₁`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L133) with integral $q$-expansions $p_f,p_g$, $p_g\neq 0$, and every $x\in K$ whose Laurent expansion is the image of $p_f/p_g$, one has, after applying any embedding $\iota$ with $\iota\zeta=e^{2\pi i/q}$, the identity $\iota(\tau x)\cdot q\text{-}\mathrm{exp}(g\mid_k\mathrm{conjElemN}\,q\,\gamma^{-1})=q\text{-}\mathrm{exp}(f\mid_k\mathrm{conjElemN}\,q\,\gamma^{-1})$.
--
--   Under these hypotheses the conclusion is the conjunction of two statements.
--
--   First: for every prime ideal $Q$ of $B$ containing the image of $\varpi$ there exist $\gamma\in\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb Z)$ with $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)$ and $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$, and $\tau\in\mathrm{Aut}_L(K)$ with `IsLevelAutAt L q ζ q (q^2*M') H₁ γ⁻¹ K τ`, such that every $b\in B$ lying in $\mathfrak m_W$ satisfies $\tau(b)\in B$, and, as an element of $B$, $\tau(b)$ lies in $Q$; that is, $\tau(\mathfrak m_W\cap B)\subseteq Q$.
--
--   Second: for every $b\in B$, if for all $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ and all $\tau$ with `IsLevelAutAt L q ζ q (q^2*M') H₁ γ⁻¹ K τ` such that $\tau(b)\in B$ the element $\tau(b)$ lies in $\mathfrak m_W$, then the image of $\varpi$ in $B$ divides $b$.
--
--   This is the transitivity-and-reducedness step for the blow-up chart $B=C[J/\varpi_t]$ of the integral model at a supersingular point: the level automorphisms attached to $\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ carry $\mathfrak m_W\cap B$ into every prime of $B$ above $\varpi$, and an element of $B$ lying in all the corresponding valuation ideals is divisible by $\varpi$. It is the variant adapted to the auxiliary level $H_1$ cut out by the congruences modulo $q$ and modulo the guard prime $\ell$, valid without the restriction $q\ge 5$, and it feeds the decomposition of the Drinfeld fibre of the blow-up chart under the level automorphisms.
